<section class="event-details-section pt-5">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-title-box">
      <div class="section-tagline">Breaking Barriers: A Milestone for "Made in Rwanda" and Intra-African Trade!</div>
    </div>
    <hr>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-lg-12">
        <div class="event-details-content-box">
          <p>Today marks a historic leap toward Africa’s industrialization and economic integration! We are thrilled to announce the Certification of 32 Rwandan SMEs and the signing of landmark Mutual Recognition Agreements (MRAs) between the Rwanda Standards Board (RSB), the Standards Association of Zimbabwe, and the Agence Congolaise de Normalisation et de la Qualité (ACONOQ).</p>
          <hr>
          <h4>🏆 Empowering Our SMEs: </h4>
          <hr>
          <p>A total of 32 local industries have officially received continental quality certificates covering 72 diverse products —ranging from agriculture and food processing to value-added goods.</p>
          <hr><br>
          <h4>🤝 What this means? </h4>
          <p>These SMEs can now export across Africa without the delays of additional testing or re-certification.<br><br>Strengthening Regional Ties by signing MRAs with Zimbabwe and the Republic of Congo, we are moving from dialogue to action. These agreements embody the vision of “One Standard, One Test, One Certificate Accepted Everywhere,” significantly reducing technical barriers to trade and fostering trust across our borders.</p>
          <p>Together, we are building a more integrated, industrialised, and prosperous Africa!</p>
